Opensource software shouldnt block the user from editing files on their own computer.

I propose ignoring all editing permissions on all files. Granting the user the power to make their own choices.

all permission methods call Permissions::bit(). To make those methods always allow printing, copying, editing, annotations, forms and page assembly

https://github.com/storytold/printcraft/blob/55c581760ab389b88f08997ab235eecdf1a1b002/crates/crypt/src/lib.rs#L94

fn bit(&self, n: u32) -> bool {
    self.owner || (self.bits >> (n - 1)) & 1 == 1
}

change to 

fn bit(&self, _n: u32) -> bool {
    true
}

Works great and I can now edit my files without my computer trying to tell me what I can and cannot do.

