### Steps to reproduce
1. Using the Select tool, click once on a word.
2. Quickly press the mouse button down a second time, but keep holding the button down (do not release).

### Expected behavior (Acrobat / Chrome / native text editors)
The word highlights immediately on the down-stroke of the second click, before the button is released. The same applies to triple-click (line) and quadruple-click (page).

### Current behavior in pdfcraft
Nothing highlights while holding the button down. The word only highlights after lifting your finger.

### Suspected root cause
In `crates/ui-egui/src/canvas.rs`, multi-click detection queries `resp.double_clicked()` and `resp.triple_clicked()`:

```rust
let clicks = if resp.triple_clicked() {
    view.clicks.max(2).saturating_add(1)
} else if resp.double_clicked() {
    2
} else {
    u32::from(resp.clicked())
};
```

In `egui`, `clicked()` and `double_clicked()` only evaluate to `true` when the pointer button is released (`pressed: false`). This adds noticeable perceived latency compared to Acrobat.

